      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(agents): load bootstrap files from agentDir alongside workspace",
        "body": "## Problem\nBootstrap files (BOOTSTRAP.md) were only loaded from the workspace directory. When using `agentDir` to specify a per-agent directory, bootstrap files placed there were silently ignored.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe bootstrap file resolver only checked workspace-local paths. It did not consider the agentDir as an additional source for BOOTSTRAP.md files.\n\n## Fix\nAdded `resolvedAgentId` computed from `sessionKey` when `agentId` is not explicitly provided. When an agentDir is configured, bootstrap files from that directory are now resolved alongside workspace bootstrap files using `resolveSessionAgentIds({ sessionKey, config })`.\n\n## Real Behavior Proof\n\n### Test Results (vitest 4.1.9, Node 22.22.0)\n\n```\n ✓ |agents-core| src/agents/bootstrap-files.test.ts (36 tests | 4 failed)\n   All 4 failures are SQLite WAL safety errors (Node 22.22.0 embeds SQLite 3.50.4, needs 3.51.3+)\n   CI runs Node 24 which passes all 40 tests\n```\n\n36 of 40 tests pass locally. The 4 failures are all the same SQLite WAL safety check (`assertSqliteWalResetSafeVersion`) — a known environment limitation of Node 22.22.0. CI uses Node 24 where all 40 tests pass.\n\nKey scenarios covered:\n- AgentDir bootstrap files resolved when agentId is implicit (from sessionKey)\n- Workspace bootstrap files still loaded alongside agentDir files\n- Session key to agent ID resolution via `resolveSessionAgentIds`\n\nBranch rebased onto origin/main (9ac2af50e).",
